OL,3,AGerman Chancellor Merz calls state
OL,4,Aelection a 'disaster' for his party but
OL,5,Avows to stay on
OL,6,
OL,7,FEmbattled German Chancellor Friedrich
OL,8,FMerz has vowed to stay on despite exit
OL,9,Fpolls in two local elections suggesting
OL,10,Fdamaging defeats for his centre-right
OL,11,FChristian Democratic Union (CDU) party.
OL,13,FIn the north-eastern state of
OL,14,FMecklenburg-Vorpommern, the party was
OL,15,Fprojected to only just scrape into
OL,16,Fparliament, while the AfD was on track
OL,17,Fto win the most votes. Merz called the
OL,18,Fresult "a disaster" for his party.
OL,20,FIn Berlin, the ruling CDU was also
OL,21,Fexpected to be beaten by Die Linke (The
OL,22,FLeft).
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
